  pages:
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c9f68e6b2a1e5ab4b94e1962285423ab, type: 3}
    description: 'To use the circle, rectangle, line, or selection tools, click on
      two points on the grid.

      On PC, the small dot in the top-left corner
      indicates the mouse position.'
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1ded4a904ddf0d64fbfe55dedf147a0b, type: 3}
    description: 'After selecting an area, use the arrows in the bottom-left corner
      to move it.

      Press the center button to confirm the movement and finish
      the tool.'
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 37c2f38c97e1d11478132e1b240704c9, type: 3}
    description: 'The quick save button is used for artwork that has already been
      saved or loaded.

      The set it belongs to will be displayed just below
      the button.'
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6c6d490bef29cf845a7d485cb3d6e86c, type: 3}
    description: 'When clicking Save, the available sets will be shown next. Click
      the desired set again to confirm saving.

      In the top-right corner, you
      can create a new set.

      To delete, click Delete, select the desired set,
      and confirm the action.'
